sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client
  participant API as Auth API
  participant RL as Rate Limit And Cooldown
  participant Redis as Redis Lookup And OTP
  participant Mongo as MongoDB
  participant Mail as Mail Queue
  participant Token as Token Service
  participant OAuth as OAuth Provider

  rect rgb(245, 248, 255)
    Note over Client,Mail: Register
    Client->>API: POST /auth/register
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit
    API->>API: Validate and canonicalize email
    Note over API,Redis: If bitmap:v1 is not ready, fallback to MongoDB pre-check
    API->>Redis: GETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 when ready
    alt BIT = 0
      API->>Redis: Store pending registration and OTP
      API->>Mail: Send registration OTP
      API-->>Client: OTP sent
    else BIT = 1
      API->>Redis: GET user:email:{hash}
      alt Cache hit
        API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
      else Cache miss
        API->>Mongo: Find user by email
        alt User exists
          API->>Redis: SET user cache
          API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
        else User missing
          API->>Redis: Store pending registration and OTP
          API->>Mail: Send registration OTP
          API-->>Client: OTP sent
        end
      end
    end

    Client->>API: POST /auth/register/verify-otp
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit
    API->>Redis: Verify OTP and load pending registration
    Redis-->>API: Pending canonical email
    API->>Mongo: Create user under unique email index
    alt Create succeeds
      API->>Redis: SET user cache, SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1, DEL negative cache
      API->>Redis: Delete registration OTP state
      API-->>Client: Account verified
    else Duplicate key
      API->>Redis: Delete stale registration OTP state
      API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
    end
  end

  rect rgb(247, 252, 247)
    Note over Client,Token: Login
    Client->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit
    API->>API: Validate canonical email and exact password
    API->>Redis: GET user:email:{hash}
    alt Cache hit
      API->>Mongo: Load auth fields by userId
    else Cache miss
      API->>Mongo: Load auth fields by canonical email
      alt User found
        API->>Redis: SET user cache and SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1
      end
    end
    alt User missing
      API->>API: Dummy bcrypt compare
      API-->>Client: 401 Invalid email or password
    else User found
      API->>API: Verify password hash
      alt Password invalid
        API-->>Client: 401 Invalid email or password
      else Password valid
        API->>Token: Issue access token with tokenVersion and refresh token
        API-->>Client: Login success
      end
    end
  end

  rect rgb(255, 250, 245)
    Note over Client,Mail: Forgot Password And Reset
    Client->>API: POST /auth/password/forgot
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit and email cooldown
    API->>API: Validate canonical email
    Note over API,Redis: If bitmap:v1 is not ready or lookup fails, fallback to MongoDB
    API->>Redis: GETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 when ready
    alt BIT = 0
      API-->>Client: Generic accepted response
    else BIT = 1
      API->>Redis: GET user cache then negative cache
      alt Negative cache hit
        API-->>Client: Generic accepted response
      else Need database check
        API->>Mongo: Find user by canonical email
        alt User missing
          API->>Redis: SET negative cache
          API-->>Client: Generic accepted response
        else User exists
          API->>Redis: SET user cache, SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1, store forgot OTP
          API->>Mail: Send forgot-password OTP
          API-->>Client: Generic accepted response
        end
      end
    end

    Client->>API: POST /auth/password/verify-otp
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit
    API->>Redis: Verify forgot OTP
    alt OTP valid
      API->>Redis: Store reset token
      API-->>Client: Reset token issued
    else OTP invalid
      API-->>Client: Existing OTP failure
    end

    Client->>API: POST /auth/password/reset
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit
    API->>Redis: Verify reset token
    API->>Mongo: Load user and update password
    API->>Token: Revoke all sessions by tokenVersion
    API->>Redis: Delete reset state and invalidate auth cache
    API-->>Client: Password reset success
  end

  rect rgb(250, 247, 255)
    Note over Client,Mail: Authenticated Password And Email Change
    Client->>API: POST /auth/password/change-request
    API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit and user cooldown
    API->>Mongo: Load user and verify old password
    API->>Redis: Store pending password change and OTP
    API->>Mail: Send OTP to current email
    API-->>Client: OTP sent

    Client->>API: POST /auth/password/change-verify
    API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
    API->>Redis: Verify change-password OTP and pending state
    API->>Mongo: Update password
    API->>Token: Revoke all sessions by tokenVersion
    API->>Redis: Delete change-password state and invalidate auth cache
    API-->>Client: Password changed

    Client->>API: POST /auth/email/change-request
    API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
    API->>RL: Auth rate limit and user cooldown
    API->>API: Validate canonical new email
    Note over API,Redis: If bitmap:v1 is not ready, fallback to MongoDB pre-check
    API->>Redis: GETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 for new email when ready
    alt BIT = 1
      API->>Redis: GET user cache
      API->>Mongo: Check new email if cache misses
    end
    alt New email already exists
      API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
    else New email available
      API->>Redis: Store old and new email OTPs
      API->>Mail: Send OTPs to old and new emails
      API-->>Client: OTPs sent
    end

    Client->>API: POST /auth/email/change-verify
    API->>Token: Authenticate access token and tokenVersion
    API->>Redis: Verify old and new email OTPs
    API->>Mongo: Update email under unique index
    alt Update succeeds
      API->>Token: Revoke all sessions by tokenVersion
      API->>Redis: DEL old user cache, SET new user cache, SETBIT new bitmap, DEL new negative cache
      API-->>Client: Email changed
    else Duplicate key
      API-->>Client: 409 Email already exists
    end
  end

  rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over Client,Token: Token And OAuth
    Client->>API: POST /auth/refresh-token
    API->>Token: Verify refresh JWT and persisted refresh-token record
    API->>Mongo: Load current tokenVersion
    API->>Token: Issue new access token
    API-->>Client: Token refreshed

    Client->>API: POST /auth/logout
    API->>Token: Revoke current refresh token and blacklist access token
    API-->>Client: Logged out

    Client->>API: POST /auth/logout-all
    API->>Token: Authenticate access token
    API->>Token: Revoke all refresh tokens and increment tokenVersion
    API-->>Client: Logged out all sessions

    Client->>API: GET /auth/oauth/:provider
    API->>OAuth: Redirect to provider authorize URL
    OAuth-->>Client: Provider login page
    Client->>API: GET /auth/callback
    API->>OAuth: Exchange code and load profile
    API->>Mongo: Find, link, or create user
    API->>Redis: SET user cache, SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1, DEL negative cache
    API->>Token: Issue access and refresh tokens
    API-->>Client: Redirect to frontend callback
  end
